  "seoTitle": "PT Fonusa Agung Mulia Factory Fire Victims Identified",
  "metaDescription": "Authorities confirm 24 bodies have been recovered from the PT Fonusa Agung Mulia fire in Serang, as identification efforts using DNA testing continue.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Search and rescue teams have recovered 24 body bags from the site of the PT Fonusa Agung Mulia factory fire in Cikande.",
    "Identification of the victims is expected to take several weeks and will involve DNA testing at the Bhayangkara Hospital.",
    "Regency officials confirmed that the affected workers are entitled to compensation and coverage through the BPJS Ketenagakerjaan social security program."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "A major fire recently struck the PT Fonusa Agung Mulia candy factory located in the Cikande district of Serang, Indonesia. Following the incident, emergency services successfully recovered 24 sets of remains from the facility, which have been transported to Bhayangkara Hospital for processing. Local authorities, including the Regent of Serang, Ratu Zakiyah, have publicly stated that the workers involved will receive full support and benefits through the national social security system, BPJS Ketenagakerjaan. Identification of the victims remains an ongoing process, with officials estimating that DNA analysis could take between two to three weeks to complete. Emergency response efforts remain a priority for the Banten regional government, as investigators continue to evaluate the site and manage the recovery operation. The incident has drawn significant public and media attention due to the high number of casualties and the ongoing search for other missing persons.",
